# .vinaya/doc-owners — code → doc bindings for the coherence seam.
#
# Format: one binding per line, CODEOWNERS-shaped.
#     <code-glob>  <doc-pointer>
# Whitespace-separated. Lines starting with `#` and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Glob syntax (kept deliberately simple — no character classes):
#   `**`  matches any sequence (including `/`)
#   `*`   matches any sequence not containing `/`
#   every other character is literal — so Next.js dynamic-route segments
#   like `[username]` match literally, no escaping required.
#
# Pointer forms:
#   in-repo path             e.g. `.claude/skills/ui-components/SKILL.md`
#   in-repo path with anchor e.g. `aeg-root/state-machine.md#section-9`
#   URL                      e.g. `https://example.com/docs/x`
#
# Coverage rule (enforced by C5 in `@attalabs/aeg-core`'s `verify-docs.ts`; a
# missing/unsatisfied binding below surfaces as a `C5 doc-coverage: …` error):
#   When a code file in the PR matches a glob:
#     - in-repo pointer  → that path must appear in the PR diff, else FAIL
#     - URL pointer      → require a `Doc-ack: <pointer> — <note>` PR-body line
#     - dangling pointer → in-repo pointer that does not exist on disk: FAIL
#   Escape:
#     A PR-wide `vinaya/waiver:docs` label whose labeling timeline event's actor is a
#     configured principal suppresses every fired binding for that PR — a
#     forge-authenticated human act, never a parseable string. There is no
#     PR-body waiver field; label presence alone is never sufficient.
#   Neutral-edit path (state-machine.md Section 15):
#     A fired in-repo binding whose doc is genuinely not owed — the matched
#     code diff is comment/whitespace-only, not a behavior change — is
#     satisfied by `Doc-neutral: <pointer> — <note>` in the PR body, where
#     <pointer> is the binding's doc pointer. The declaration alone never
#     passes: `evaluateC5` reads the actual diff of every matched file and
#     requires every changed (+/-) line to be blank or comment-only before
#     honoring the claim (`isMechanicallyNeutralDiff`). A declared-but-
#     unevidenced claim is a distinct failure (`C5 doc-neutral-unverified`),
#     not a silent pass — this is what keeps the escape from being self-serve.
#     Silence (no doc, no Doc-neutral, no waiver) is still always FAIL.
#
# Dormancy:
#   This file absent, OR no glob matches any changed code file → silent no-op.
#   The gate has no opinion until you teach it one.
#
# ── No-doc allow-list ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Surfaces that legitimately need no bound doc are listed below.  Format:
#   # no-doc: <glob> — <reason>
# These lines exempt the matching directory from the completeness scoreboard
# (verify-docs --full advisory output).  They do NOT affect C5 enforcement —
# if a binding exists for a surface, C5 still fires on changed files regardless
# of any no-doc line.  Use no-doc for scaffold-only, config-only, or stub-only
# surfaces where adding a doc-owners binding would be meaningless busywork.
# To un-exempt a surface, remove its no-doc line and add a real binding.
#
# no-doc: packages/typescript-config/** — pure config package; no behavior docs needed
# no-doc: packages/instrumentation/** — dev-ergonomics utility (browser-extension error
#   filter, ~85 lines); no product behavior to document. Flagged for Planner: no owning
#   skill exists (aeg-governance-hardening task 3, 2026-07-02).

